<InfoPanel Title="Demo Story" Subtitle="How to explain the project in one short walkthrough.">
    <ChildContent>
        <p>
            OperationsFlow is a workflow-style business system prototype for capturing operational follow-up work,
            assigning ownership, attaching evidence, reviewing pressure, and producing traceable management outputs.
            It is not just a dashboard. It shows the path from scattered work to accountable records, evidence,
            data quality checks, reports, and future Microsoft 365 implementation.
        </p>
    </ChildContent>
</InfoPanel>

<InfoPanel Title="Demo Route" Subtitle="Recommended route for a portfolio walkthrough.">
    <ChildContent>
        <ol>
            <li>
                <strong>Dashboard:</strong> Start with the system overview and explain the problem:
                scattered work across emails, paper notes, spreadsheets, and conversations.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Work Orders:</strong> Show operational work, owners, priority, status, due dates,
                file counts, details, attachments, and activity history.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Corrective Actions:</strong> Show follow-up actions, source-linked context, close-out
                evidence, and links from risk/training/document issues.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Document Intake:</strong> Show incoming document workflow, details pages, attached source
                files, and how intake records feed reminders/reports/data quality.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Document Library:</strong> Show one evidence register across Work Orders, Corrective
                Actions, and Document Intake, using the local storage provider.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Data Quality:</strong> Show missing evidence checks, overdue work, weak records,
                compliance flags, and links back to the source records.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Reports:</strong> Show management action rows, evidence coverage, missing evidence
                reporting, training compliance, document reviews, and workload pressure.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Activity Log:</strong> Finish with traceability: created, updated, uploaded, deleted,
                and reviewed events.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </ChildContent>
</InfoPanel>

<InfoPanel Title="What To Say" Subtitle="Plain-English reviewer explanation.">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Business Context</strong>
                <span>
                    OperationsFlow captures follow-up work before it disappears into emails, paper notes,
                    spreadsheets, or someone’s memory.
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Workflow Context</strong>
                <span>
                    Records are owned, prioritised, tracked, reviewed, linked to evidence, and surfaced in
                    management views.
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Evidence Context</strong>
                <span>
                    Week 3 adds local document storage, record attachments, evidence counts, missing evidence
                    checks, and reporting coverage.
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Technical Context</strong>
                <span>
                    The local storage provider is a proof layer that can be swapped for SharePoint/Microsoft Graph
                    in Week 4.
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Portfolio Context</strong>
                <span>
                    The project demonstrates systems thinking, not just UI layout: workflow, data model, evidence,
                    reporting, traceability, and boundaries.
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Boundary Context</strong>
                <span>
                    The current version is still a local SQLite prototype. Production rollout needs auth,
                    permissions, SharePoint storage, deployment, and operational ownership.
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
</InfoPanel>

