<InfoPanel Title="Week 3 Demo Focus" Subtitle="What changed in the production foundation sprint.">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Local Storage</strong>
                <span>Files are stored locally through a storage service abstraction.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Record Attachments</strong>
                <span>Work Orders, Corrective Actions, and Document Intake can upload evidence directly from details pages.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Document Library</strong>
                <span>All active files appear in one searchable cross-module library.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Evidence Counts</strong>
                <span>Workflow register pages show whether key records already have files attached.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Data Quality</strong>
                <span>Priority or overdue records without evidence are now flagged.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="of-review-proof-card">
                <strong>Reports</strong>
                <span>Management reporting now includes evidence coverage and missing evidence rows.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Boundary Notes" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
    <ul>
        <li>This page is part of the portfolio review layer.</li>
        <li>The current app uses local SQLite demo data and local file storage.</li>
        <li>Production rollout still needs authentication, role permissions, audit retention, Microsoft 365 integration, backups, and operational ownership.</li>
        <li>Week 4 should replace the local storage proof with SharePoint/Microsoft Graph storage while keeping the same workflow pages.</li>
    </ul>
</GuidanceNote>